 "background": [
  {
   "text": "Electrical heating protects the flight compartment windows (hot air protects slats and engine intakes).",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-30-10-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1766
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Electrical heating anti-ices each windshield and defogs the cockpit side windows. Two independent WHCs, one on each side, regulate the system, protect it against overheating and indicate faults.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-30-40-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1782
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Window heating comes ON automatically when at least one engine is running or in flight, and manually before engine start when PROBE/WINDOW HEAT is switched ON.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-30-40-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1782
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The windshield heats at low power on ground and normal power in flight; the windows have only one heating level.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-30-40-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1782
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "PROBE/WINDOW HEAT pb: AUTO = heated in flight, or on ground with one engine running (except TAT probes). ON = blue light, probes and windows heated permanently. Ensure the probe covers are removed before selecting ON.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-30-50-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 1788
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Two different C/B sets: the reset uses the WHC C/Bs X13 / W13 (ANTI ICE / WHC / 1 / 2); the arcing procedure pulls the heating C/Bs ANTI ICE/WINDOWS L X14 / R W14 (122VU) or L/R WSHLD AF10 / AF03 (123VU).",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "QRH",
     "code": "02.09",
     "page": "02.09A",
     "pdf": 62
    },
    {
     "book": "QRH",
     "code": "25.05",
     "page": "25.05A",
     "pdf": 223
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
